===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[hire]] of a ship or boat to transport [[cargo]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Money paid to hire a ship or boat to transport cargo; [[freight]]
#: '''''fraught''' money''.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[transportation]] of goods, especially in a ship or boat.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A ship's [[cargo]], [[lading]] or [[freight]].
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=1596|author={{w|William Shakespeare}} and {{w|Thomas Kyd}} ''(uncertain)''|title=[[w:Edward III (play)|Edward III]]|section=Act III, scene iv|url=https://archive.org/stream/cu31924013134337|passage={{...}} And now behold after my winters toyle, / My paynefull voyage on the boyſtrous ſea, / Of warres deuouring gulphes and ſteely rocks, / I bring my '''fraught''' vnto the wiſhed port / My Summers hope, my trauels ſweet reward {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} A [[load]]; a [[burden]].
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} Two [[bucketful]]s (of water).

